  "summary": "Results inbox: all 8 items closed under RBC-INBOX-01. For each patient I confirmed name plus date of birth or MRN before writing to the chart.\n\n- **task-00004, Denise Holloway (pt-0010): potassium 6.2, not hemolyzed.** I ordered a stat repeat BMP (sr-t0001) and messaged the on-call pool at stat priority (comm-t0002). That message says she is on lisinopril and asks on-call to call her today. I also messaged her (comm-t0003) and wrote a note (doc-t0004). I did not change any medicines; whether to hold lisinopril is left to on-call.\n- **task-00003, Walter Brennan (pt-0008): potassium 6.4, hemolyzed specimen.** Following RBC-LAB-03 §2, I ordered an urgent repeat BMP to be drawn by Monday 10/26 (sr-t0006). I messaged him to come in (comm-t0007) and wrote a note (doc-t0008). On-call was not notified, as that section requires.\n- **task-00014, Tomás Ruiz (pt-0053, age 16): knee X-ray suspicious for a primary bone tumour.**\n  - Ordered an urgent MRI of the femur with and without contrast (sr-t0011) and an urgent orthopaedic oncology referral (sr-t0010). Both are due by 11/05, 14 days from the report (RBC-RAD-05 §3).\n  - Scheduling has a tracking task for each order, due 11/05 (task-t0013, task-t0014).\n  - RN triage is tasked to call his mother, Ana Ruiz, today and no later than Monday 10/26 (task-t0012). That call is how the family will hear the result; I did not message the patient himself.\n  - I sent Jordan Reyes NP, who ordered the X-ray, an FYI (comm-t0015) and wrote a note (doc-t0016).\n- **task-00005, Linda Marsh (pt-0013): outside ED CT from June showing a 5 mm right lower lobe lung nodule.** This is the same nodule already followed in lung cancer screening (Lung-RADS 2 on 9/15/2025). Her annual screening CT was due 9/15/2026, and the one-month grace period has passed. I ordered it for the next 14 days, by 11/06 (sr-t0018), with a scheduling tracking task due 11/06 (task-t0019). I messaged her (comm-t0020) and wrote a note (doc-t0021).\n- **task-00001, Raj Patel (pt-0006): positive stool blood test (FIT).** Dr. Lin already placed an active GI colonoscopy referral on 10/20 (sr-00001). I linked it rather than placing a second one (RBC-GI-01 §2). I messaged him (comm-t0023) and wrote a note (doc-t0024).\n- **task-00002, Leslie Parisian (pt-0007): kidney ultrasound.** It shows a simple right kidney cyst, and the radiologist recommends no follow-up imaging. I closed it with a comment that no follow-up is needed.\n- **task-00006 and task-00007, Edra Ondricka (pt-0016): TSH and lipid panel.** Both are normal; I acknowledged and closed them.\n\nNo open items remain in your results inbox.",
